PUBLIC AGGREGATE REFERENCE DATA
The bank/derived.npz empirical distributions and cohort-mean shapes derive from
FairFace, "FairFace: Face Attribute Dataset for Balanced Race, Gender, and Age"
(Karkkainen and Joo, WACV 2021), distributed under CC BY 4.0:
https://github.com/joojs/fairface
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
These transformed reference statistics retain the FairFace attribution and
CC BY 4.0 terms. Apache-2.0 does not replace the dataset's license.
Changes: model-based landmark measurement; cohort grouping and identity-cluster
counting; independent empirical CDF threshold/count pairs; cohort mean shapes and
held-out distance distributions; suppression of cohorts below the existing
150-cluster floor and distributions with fewer than50finite observations.
No reference photographs, individual reference landmark meshes, row identities,
per-person pose arrays or identity-cluster IDs are distributed. Cohort labels
are FairFace annotators' labels, not verified participant self-descriptions.
This representation is not a formal differential-privacy or anonymity guarantee.

MEDIAPIPE
Google MediaPipe source is Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe
Model assets are downloaded directly from checksum-pinned official Google URLs
before photo intake; model weights are not included in the app or source tree.
The auxiliary six-class forehead model is selfie_multiclass_256x256 float32 v1:
https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/image_segmenter/selfie_multiclass_256x256/float32/1/selfie_multiclass_256x256.tflite
Model card (Google / Adel Ahmadyan, May2023, Apache2.0):
https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-assets/Model%20Card%20Multiclass%20Segmentation.pdf
The app uses it for hair/skin visibility; it does not establish hidden anatomy.

BUNDLED RUNTIME AND LIBRARIES
The macOS app includes CPython and installed Python dependencies. Their own
copyright/license files remain in the runtime distribution, including the
site-packages dist-info license directories. Dependencies include MediaPipe,
NumPy, SciPy, OpenCV, Matplotlib, Pydantic, limits and cryptography.
Python standalone runtime source/build project:
https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone
No third-party library is relicensed by the application license.

